---
interface Props {
  // 'full' renders every question (used on /faq).
  // 'subset' renders a 4-question homepage subset with a link to /faq,
  // and the FAQPage JSON-LD covers only the visible questions (no verbatim
  // duplication of the full set across two URLs).
  variant?: 'full' | 'subset';
}

const { variant = 'full' } = Astro.props;

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'What is CardHabit?',
    a: 'CardHabit is a daily card draw for your life, made for people who read Atomic Habits, tried 75 Hard, and want a system they can sustain instead of one that burns them out. Every morning it deals you five habit cards, and you commit to the ones you can handle. Every card you finish goes into your binder, a growing collection of the days you showed up.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What kind of app is CardHabit?',
    a: 'CardHabit is an iOS daily challenge app built on trading-card-game mechanics: every morning it deals you five habit cards, and you commit to what you can handle that day. The cards come first. Rank and XP sit quietly underneath as a progression layer, and the habits are what the daily deal leaves behind.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Who is CardHabit for?',
    a: 'CardHabit is for people who read Atomic Habits and want a system instead of willpower, and for people who did 75 Hard, burned out, and want something sustainable that still feels real. If you want a daily practice you can keep up for years, with friends dealt in instead of grinding alone, it was built for you.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is this another 75 Hard?',
    a: 'No, and the difference is the point. 75 Hard asks for extreme things once, over a 75-day pass-or-fail run. CardHabit asks for hard things every day: each card is scoped small enough to actually do every morning and hard enough to feel real, and the system survives missed days instead of sending you back to Day 1.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What if I miss a day?',
    a: 'Your streak counts on days you finish what you committed to. If you miss a day, that streak ends and a new one starts the next morning. There is no purity test and no restart-from-zero penance, and the cards already in your binder stay there. The whole system is built to survive missed days rather than punish you for being human.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How does the daily draw work?',
    a: 'Every morning you are dealt five cards. You hold a card to commit to it: two cards a day on the free tier, all five on Pro. Each card you finish fills a slot in your binder, the collection the app calls the Codex. Rarer cards carry a richer printed finish, from plain to a foil edge to full gold foil.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What are the suits?',
    a: 'With CardHabit 2.0, the deck has five suits: Physical, Mind, Nutrition, Recovery, and Connection, plus the Joker, a wild card that can ask for anything (the base deck holds two). Connection is new in 2.0 and covers the people in your life. The current app deals from the earlier set of categories until 2.0 arrives.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What can your friends actually do?',
    a: 'Coming in CardHabit 2.0, you can deal a friend in. From any card in your hand, you deal the same card into a friend\'s hand for today, by share link if they do not have the app yet. If you both finish it, you each get a paired foil card with both names on it in your binders. If one of you does not finish, nothing bad happens.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What if a friend deals me a card I cannot do today?',
    a: 'Then you leave it. A dealt card is an invitation, not an obligation: it does not replace your own hand, it does not count against your streak, and the friend who dealt it loses nothing. You only commit to what you can handle that day.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is CardHabit available now?',
    a: 'Yes. CardHabit launched on the iOS App Store in July 2026. Download the app today and draw your first hand of cards tomorrow morning.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What does CardHabit cost?',
    a: 'The free tier covers the daily draw and lets you commit to two cards a day. CardHabit Pro unlocks all five daily commits and the full record of everything you have played, with a 7-day free trial. Founder pricing is live in the app now: $4.99 a month or $39.99 a year, locked in at signup for as long as your subscription stays active.',
  },
  // 2.11: moved below the substantive questions (what it is, the 75 Hard
  // difference, pricing). Disambiguation trivia shouldn't be the first
  // thing a reader hits. Content unchanged.
  {
    q: 'Is CardHabit the same as Habit Card or cardhabit.com?',
    a: 'No. CardHabit is the iOS app that deals you five habit cards every morning, and its only website is cardhabitapp.com. It is not affiliated with cardhabit.com, and it is not Habit Card, a tile-grid tracker. The App Store listing is CardHabit: TCG Habit Tracker (id 6768107296).',
  },
];

const subsetQuestions = [
  'What is CardHabit?',
  'Is CardHabit the same as Habit Card or cardhabit.com?',
  'Is this another 75 Hard?',
  'What does CardHabit cost?',
];

const visibleFaqs =
  variant === 'subset' ? faqs.filter((f) => subsetQuestions.includes(f.q)) : faqs;

const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: visibleFaqs.map((item) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: item.q,
    acceptedAnswer: {
      '@type': 'Answer',
      text: item.a,
    },
  })),
};
---

<section class="section-pad">
  <div style="max-width:780px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 1.5rem;">

    <!-- Eyebrow -->
    <p class="fade-in" style="font-family:'Jost',system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:10px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:0.28em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6E1E22;margin:0 0 1.25rem;text-align:center;">
      The details
    </p>

    <!-- H2 -->
    <h2 class="fade-in" style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',Georgia,serif;font-weight:500;font-size:clamp(2rem,6vw,3rem);line-height:1.08;letter-spacing:-0.01em;color:#2B211B;margin:0 0 3rem;text-align:center;">
      Questions, answered.
    </h2>

    <!-- FAQ list -->
    <div style="max-width:640px;margin:0 auto;">
      {visibleFaqs.map((item, i) => (
        <div
          class="fade-in"
          style={`padding:2rem 0;${i > 0 ? 'border-top:0.5px solid rgba(156, 122, 46, 0.18);' : ''}`}
        >
          <h3 style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',Georgia,serif;font-weight:500;font-size:1.4rem;line-height:1.3;color:#2B211B;margin:0 0 0.75rem;">
            {item.q}
          </h3>
          <p style="font-family:'Jost',system-ui,sans-serif;font-weight:300;font-size:0.98rem;line-height:1.7;color:#574B40;margin:0;">
            {item.a}
          </p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>

    {variant === 'subset' && (
      <p style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',Georgia,serif;font-style:italic;font-size:1.25rem;line-height:1.6;color:#574B40;margin:2.5rem 0 0;text-align:center;">
        <a href="/faq" style="color:#6E1E22;text-decoration:none;border-bottom:0.5px solid rgba(156, 122, 46, 0.4);">More questions, answered on the FAQ page</a>
      </p>
    )}

  </div>
</section>

<!-- FAQPage structured data -->
<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} />
